{title: In the Garden}
{artist: C. Austin Miles}
{genre: Gospel, Hymn}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 9/8}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [G]come to the garden alone
While the [D]dew is still on the [G]roses
And the [G]voice I hear, falling on my ear
The [C]Son of God dis[D]closes[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And He [G]walks with me, and He talks with me
And He [D]tells me I am His [G]own
And the [G]joy we share as we tarry there
[C]None other has ever [G]known
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He [G]speaks, and the sound of His voice
Is so [D]sweet the birds hush their [G]singing
And the [G]melody that He gave to me
With[C]in my heart is [D]ringing[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'd [G]stay in the garden with Him
Though the [D]night around me be [G]falling
But He [G]bids me go, through the voice of woe
His [C]voice to me is [D]calling[G]
{end_of_verse}
